-snip">George Monck was an English soldier who fought for the king and then for Parliament and was Cromwell's commander in Scotland in the 1650s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/george-of-antioch"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/george-of-antioch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">George of Antioch</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">George of Antioch was a Greek Christian who served the Zirid rulers of Mahdia before becoming the leading minister and admiral of Roger II of Sicily, with the title…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">George of Poděbrady</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">George of Poděbrady was a Utraquist Hussite nobleman who governed Bohemia as regent for Ladislaus the Posthumous and was elected king in 1458.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/george-of-saxony"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/george-of-saxony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">George of Saxony</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">George of Saxony, called the Bearded, was Duke of Saxony from 1500 to 1539 and a firm opponent of Martin Luther.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/george-pocock"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/george-pocock.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">George Pocock</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sir George Pocock was a British admiral.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/george-pomeroy-colley"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/george-pomeroy-colley.jpg